("steps",[("Step 1","Identify the base adjective and the persons/things compared."),("Step 2","For a superlative → comparative, use 'than any other + singular noun'."),("Step 3","For a negative positive ('not so…as'), switch the positions of the two items in the comparative."),("Step 4","Check 'the' (superlative), 'than' (comparative), 'as…as' (positive).")]),
("note","IMPORTANT","Common mistakes: (1) *This is the most unique idea* → **a unique idea**. (2) *He is more intelligent than any boy in the class* → **any other boy**. (3) *She is more taller than me* → **taller than I**. (4) *Anil is stronger than Sunil is* (fine) vs *Anil is the stronger of the two* (use 'the' with comparative when 'of the two' is present). (5) *He is junior than me* → **junior to me**. (6) *The Nile is the longest than all rivers* → **the longest of all rivers**."),
